beauty and perfection.\nHermann Weyl\nAn important problem in mathematics is to determine the symmetries of objects.\nThe objects we are interested in might be concrete things such as planar shapes,\nhigher-dimensional solids, or the universe. Or they might be more abstract, such as\ngroups, spaces of functions, or electric ﬁelds.\nWe’ll begin in this ofﬁce hour with a general discussion of groups; the focus will\nbe on interpreting every group as a group of symmetries of some object. In the\nsecond ofﬁce hour we will make precise what it means for a group to be a group\nof symmetries of an object. These ideas are at the very heart of geometric group\ntheory, the study of groups, spaces, and the interactions between them.\nSymmetry.\nBy understanding the symmetries of an object we come closer to fully\nunderstanding the object itself. For instance, consider a cube in Euclidean 3–space:\nFor general queries, contact webmaster@press.princeton.edu--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGroups | Office Hours with a Geometric Group Theorist | Princeton Scholarship Online | Oxford Academic (https://doi.org/10.23943/princeton/9780691158662.003.0001)\nciteturn624search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; Office Hours with a Geometric Group TheoristDan Margalit (ed.), Matt Clay (ed.) ...      * Collapse Office Hour One Groups ... These ideas are at the very heart of geometric group theory, the study of groups, spaces, and the interactions between them.\n\nOffice Hours with a Geometric Group Theorist\n\nDan Margalit (ed.), Matt Clay (ed.)\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.23943/princeton/9780691158662.001.0001\n\nPublished:\n\n11 July 2017\n\nOnline ISBN:\n\n9781400885398\n\nPrint ISBN:\n\n9780691158662\n\n[Input: Search in this book] Search in this book\n\nBuy on Amazon\n\n### Contents\n\n[Input]\n\n  1. Expand Front Matter\n\n  2. Collapse Part 1 Groups and Spaces\n\n     * Collapse Office Hour One Groups\n\n      